Every adjacent pair overlaps: **16–35 shared IDs**. Across all 1,176 age pairs, 874 share at least one ID. These are overlapping, age-selected windows from one shared bank, rather than disjoint age buckets. The term sliding window describes the overlap; the evidence does not establish a simple contiguous-index window algorithm.

